> what is the range of the square root of x plus 1 for u8 x?
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  note: "square root" of an integer: read as the floor square root, isqrt, not the real square root, sqrt(real(...)) (say "integer square root" or "real square root")
  ucas: it(x: u8) = isqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  1..16   (16 distinct values)
  values: 1..16
  fits in u5
  over all 256 points of the domain
> is the square root of x plus 1 equal to the square root of x plus 1?
  note: what does "the square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "the square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  note: what does "square root of" apply to: read as sqrt(x) + ..., not sqrt(x + ...) (say "square root of the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: that(x) = sqrt(x) + 1
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (proved by algebra: f - g simplifies to 0 over Q)
> what is the range of x for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> is x + 1 greater than x for u8 x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x + 1 > x
  ucas: show it
it(x: u8) = x + 1 > x
  -> bool
